<article class="env-definition" id="078Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/078Q">Definition <span data-tag="078Q">111.22.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. The <em>class group of $A$</em>, sometimes called the <em>Picard group of $A$</em> is the set $\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (A)$ of isomorphism classes of invertible $A$-modules endowed with a group operation defined by tensor product (see Exercise <a href="/tag/078P" data-tag="078P">111.22.2</a>). </p>
</article>